    "id": 283208,
    "ecosystem": "npm",
    "package_name": "panel-keylogger-sim",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "status": "MALWARE",
    "release_date": 1756699355,
    "detected_on": 1756699576,
    "last_updated": 1756711773,
    "reasons": [
      "The script explicitly identifies itself as a \"Keylogger Module\", creates sensitive files (hwid.txt, log.dat), runs reconnaissance commands (PowerShell Get-Process/Get-Service/Get-EventLog, netstat on port 443, ipconfig) and then requires \"./module/keylogger.js\". These actions indicate intentional credential/data capture and system discovery consistent with malware (keylogger/data exfiltration), even if some commands are only logged here. The intent and behaviors are clearly malicious.",
      "The package name/description explicitly state \"keylogger\" and the dependency/asset set matches clear malicious intent: iohook native assets (low-level input hooks), screenshot-desktop (screen capture), @primno/dpapi (access Windows DPAPI secrets), node-machine-id/ sqlite3 (identify and persist data), adm-zip/archiver (bundle data), and socket.io-client/axios (network exfiltration). The pkg targets a Windows executable (node18-win-x64), indicating bundling for end-user compromise. These indicators collectively show deliberate data-capture and exfiltration behavior consistent with a keylogger/stealer — treat as malware.",
      "The file exhibits multiple clear malicious indicators: heavy obfuscation (unicode-escaped property names and string-manipulation concatenation), explicit anti-detection comments (\"DO NOT DECRYPT... AVOID DETECTION BY WINDOWS DEFENDER\"), dynamic code execution via eval/Function, and an unusual use of require-as-parameter (loader/evasion technique). The module name (keylogger.js) plus these behaviors indicate deliberate intent to stealthily load and execute spying/keylogging functionality rather than benign code."
    ]
